WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.156 --> 00:00:05.480
Outside in the cool night, Romeo paused in a lane beside the wall of the Capulets' garden.

2
00:00:05.481 --> 00:00:08.894
"How can I go forward when my heart is back there?" he thought.

3
00:00:08.894 --> 00:00:15.144
He heard his friends calling for him as they left the dance, and somehow their laughter and clowning helped him make up his mind.

4
00:00:15.144 --> 00:00:18.208
He climbed the wall and leapt down on the other side.

5
00:00:18.208 --> 00:00:22.861
The garden was small, and above it a balcony extended from a second-floor bedroom.

6
00:00:22.862 --> 00:00:24.831
A light came on in the window.

7
00:00:24.832 --> 00:00:28.703
"What light is this?" he asked softly and quickly hid in the shadows.

8
00:00:28.703 --> 00:00:35.188
His heart leapt when he saw Juliet step out into the night, and with a smile to himself he answered his own question:

9
00:00:35.188 --> 00:00:39.153
"This light is the East, and Juliet is the sun!"

10
00:00:39.153 --> 00:00:42.934
Juliet leaned on the balcony rail, with her cheek resting on her hand.

11
00:00:42.935 --> 00:00:45.489
Deep in thought, she sighed his name.

12
00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:49.387
"Oh Romeo," she said, not seeing him below.

13
00:00:49.388 --> 00:00:54.825
"Why do you have to be named ‘Romeo'? A rose, by any other name, would smell as sweet.

14
00:00:54.825 --> 00:01:00.889
But if you won't deny your name, just swear you'll love me and I'll marry you and no longer be a Capulet."

15
00:01:00.889 --> 00:01:06.213
"My dear saint, I take you at your word," Romeo called out happily from below.

16
00:01:06.213 --> 00:01:11.959
Juliet knew who it was as soon as she heard his voice and looked down with joy to see Romeo standing there.

17
00:01:11.959 --> 00:01:15.022
She blushed and wished that she could recall her words.

18
00:01:15.022 --> 00:01:17.880
"Do you love me, in truth?" she asked.

19
00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.739
"I have given you my heart's answer before you even asked."

20
00:01:21.739 --> 00:01:26.094
"My love for you is as deep and boundless as the sea," Romeo replied.

21
00:01:26.094 --> 00:01:30.285
With this exchange, Romeo and Juliet promised their love to each other.

22
00:01:30.285 --> 00:01:39.189
Despite the danger that Romeo might be discovered by Juliet's kinsmen, they couldn't tear themselves away from each other and continued whispering under the moon.

23
00:01:39.189 --> 00:01:44.658
They both feared that this new love, so sudden and bright as lightning, might disappear as quickly.

24
00:01:44.658 --> 00:01:49.554
So they were already talking of marriage when Juliet's nurse called for her from the bedroom.

25
00:01:49.555 --> 00:01:54.641
"Tomorrow, I'll send you word about where and when we can be married," Romeo whispered urgently.

26
00:01:54.642 --> 00:02:03.895
"I'm coming," Juliet called back to her nurse, and then to Romeo she said, "Parting is such sweet sorrow, but now I must say goodnight."

27
00:02:03.895 --> 00:02:10.512
When she had disappeared from the balcony, Romeo leapt over the garden wall as lightly as if love had given him wings.

28
00:02:10.512 --> 00:02:15.332
Too excited to sleep, he hurried to a nearby monastery to find Friar Lawrence.

29
00:02:15.332 --> 00:02:20.213
The friendly monk was performing his early morning devotions when Romeo interrupted him.

30
00:02:20.213 --> 00:02:26.150
In a gush, Romeo explained everything, how he and Juliet had met and fallen in love.

31
00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:29.904
He asked the friar to marry them in secret that very afternoon.

32
00:02:29.904 --> 00:02:32.871
Friar Lawrence thought Romeo was being rash.

33
00:02:32.872 --> 00:02:34.701
"Be wise and slow.

34
00:02:34.702 --> 00:02:40.642
They stumble who run too fast," said the friar, but in the end he agreed to Romeo's request.

35
00:02:40.642 --> 00:02:45.189
He had always been fond of Romeo and believed that his love was sincere.

36
00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:53.015
Secretly, he hoped that this young love between a Montague and a Capulet might begin to heal the hatred between the two houses.

37
00:02:53.015 --> 00:02:57.642
Romeo was in high spirits as he returned from the monastery.

38
00:02:57.642 --> 00:03:03.284
He met Mercutio and Benvolio in the street, who were curious about where he had gone after the dance.

39
00:03:03.285 --> 00:03:07.022
He traded jokes with them, but cleverly avoided answering their questions.

40
00:03:07.023 --> 00:03:12.257
When Juliet's nurse approached, he said good-bye to his friends, promising to dine with them later.

41
00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:18.514
Quickly he explained to the nurse the arrangements he had made with the friar, and she left to give the news to Juliet.

42
00:03:18.514 --> 00:03:23.554
Juliet, who had been too excited to sleep all night, was waiting impatiently in her father's garden.

43
00:03:23.554 --> 00:03:28.269
When her nurse arrived, she quickly burst out, "Did you see him? What did he say?"

44
00:03:28.269 --> 00:03:34.581
"Have patience, just a minute! Oh, how my bones ache," said the nurse with a sour face.

45
00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:40.610
"I am so out of breath. All this running back and forth through the town is enough to give me a backache.

46
00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:44.109
You certainly know how to put your nurse to the test.

47
00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:47.094
I've never been asked to do such a journey so quickly.

48
00:03:47.094 --> 00:03:49.934
Even your mother, when she sends me to the market . . ."

49
00:03:49.935 --> 00:03:54.910
"My mother? I didn't ask you about my mother," said Juliet impatiently.

50
00:03:54.911 --> 00:03:57.013
"What did Romeo say?"

51
00:03:57.014 --> 00:03:59.871
"The young are so impatient," said the nurse.

52
00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:06.037
And then before Juliet could pester her with more questions, she asked, "Do you have time to go to church today?"

53
00:04:06.038 --> 00:04:08.157
"I have," said Juliet.

54
00:04:08.157 --> 00:04:15.205
"Well hurry then. Because this afternoon, at Friar Lawrence's monastery, you'll find a husband waiting to make you his wife!"

55
00:04:15.205 --> 00:04:21.705
"Oh thank you, Nurse!" said Juliet and hugged her. Then the nurse told her everything Romeo had said.

56
00:04:21.705 --> 00:04:27.681
When Juliet arrived at the church, Romeo was indeed waiting for her there with Friar Lawrence.

57
00:04:27.681 --> 00:04:32.592
They were so happy to see each other that the friar couldn't help but smile too.

58
00:04:32.593 --> 00:04:39.077
"If the richest man counted all his wealth, he would be a beggar compared to this uncountable happiness," he said.

59
00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:42.617
"Come, join hands, and I will join your souls in marriage."

60
00:04:42.618 --> 00:04:50.568
When the ceremony ended and the friar had prayed, "Heaven smile on this holy act," the young couple reluctantly said goodbye.

61
00:04:50.568 --> 00:04:58.402
They promised to meet again that night and planned where to place a ladder so that Romeo could climb up to the balcony to be with Juliet.

62
00:04:58.402 --> 00:05:03.565
That same afternoon, Tybalt was leading a group of Capulets through the city looking for Romeo.

63
00:05:03.566 --> 00:05:10.480
When he came across Benvolio and Mercutio in the city square, he insolently demanded to know where Romeo was.

64
00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:13.180
Romeo's friends quickly took offense.

65
00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:17.451
Tybalt, they could see, was planning some violence against Romeo.

66
00:05:17.451 --> 00:05:24.166
Mercutio pulled his sword, then Tybalt drew his sword, and while they were still arguing, Romeo entered the square.

67
00:05:24.166 --> 00:05:30.252
"Aha," cried Tybalt, "here comes the villain! Romeo, stand and put up your sword."

68
00:05:30.252 --> 00:05:37.498
Romeo, you must remember, was just returning from his wedding, so the old feud was the furthest thing from his mind.

69
00:05:37.498 --> 00:05:41.211
"I am no villain of yours, Tybalt," Romeo protested calmly.

70
00:05:41.212 --> 00:05:44.751
"In fact, I love the name Capulet as dearly as my own."

71
00:05:44.752 --> 00:05:53.515
Mercutio was neither a Capulet nor a Montague, but he was one of Romeo's oldest friends, and he was as impetuous and headstrong as Tybalt.

72
00:05:53.515 --> 00:05:57.903
Pushing Romeo aside, he faced Tybalt and called him a hateful, stinking dog.

73
00:05:57.904 --> 00:06:01.562
Tybalt answered with a swing of his sword, and they began to fight.

74
00:06:01.563 --> 00:06:05.253
"Stop this outrage," cried Romeo.

75
00:06:05.253 --> 00:06:12.752
"Fools, the prince will arrest you!" cried Benvolio, and together, he and Romeo rushed in to separate the two fighters.

76
00:06:12.753 --> 00:06:20.729
Romeo took hold of Mercutio's arm, but before Benvolio could restrain Tybalt, the young Capulet struck Mercutio with a thrust through the chest.

77
00:06:20.729 --> 00:06:27.157
Mercutio cried out in pain, and, seeing him collapse in Romeo's arms, Tybalt quickly turned to escape.

78
00:06:27.158 --> 00:06:30.649
Romeo could see in his friend's eyes that he was fatally wounded.

79
00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:33.498
Mercutio, too, knew he was dying.

80
00:06:33.499 --> 00:06:38.674
"A plague on both your houses!" he gasped. "I am slain."

81
00:06:38.674 --> 00:06:41.300
Romeo could not contain his rage.

82
00:06:41.301 --> 00:06:44.935
He laid Mercutio on the pavement and pulled his sword.

83
00:06:44.936 --> 00:06:48.498
"Stay, Tybalt!" he called out in a furious challenge.

84
00:06:48.499 --> 00:06:56.087
"Stay to keep my dead companion company, because, God help me, you will accompany him to the grave!"

